  "name": "0xarchive-backtest",
  "description": "Quant research and backtesting on 0xArchive data, done the way a careful desk does it: hand over a wallet, a trading idea, a tweet, a Pine or TS script, a paper, someone else's backtest, or a strategy file, and get a verdict with receipts. Reverse engineers a trader's style from their fills and scores how much of their book a strategy reproduces; tests whether a trader or a strategy is skilled or lucky. Every run goes into a trial ledger, the last months stay sealed until one candidate is committed, and nothing is called an edge until it passes costs, nulls, out-of-sample and walk-forward tests and a deflated Sharpe over every try. Uses the 0xarchive-backtest engine (0xbt) on Hyperliquid perps. Use for backtest, \"is this edge real\", test this strategy, reverse engineer this wallet, vault or trader, port this Pine script, audit this backtest, find me a strategy, or paper trade a strategy.",
